de spending against Askar; Polymarket prices the Democrat at 51%"], "rationale": "A redrawn Republican-leaning open seat meets a strongly favorable Democratic environment, and the available evidence — sparse August polls showing a dead heat to D+2, split expert ratings, even fundraising, and a market price near 51% for the Democrat — clusters around a coin-flip race with a slight Democratic edge.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling in October or a late shift in the national environment could tip this tossup toward either candidate.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": []}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd District is an open seat created by redrawing, with a Republican-leaning electorate but no incumbent on the ballot. Casey Askar and Pia Dandiya have each raised roughly $2.3 to $2.6 million, and outside groups have spent against Askar. Expert ratings split: Cook, Fox News, RealClearPolitics and The Economist call it a Tossup, several others lean Republican and flag a likely flip, and two outlets lean Democratic.\n\nPolling is thin and dates to August, with Democratic-sponsored surveys showing the race even to Dandiya up two. Polymarket prices the Democrat at about 51 percent. The national political environment favors Democrats this year, offsetting the district's Republican lean. National Democratic figures have campaigned in the district, and Dandiya is on air with an ad attacking congressional stock trading. The seat sits at the center of the House battlefield, with a narrow Democratic edge driven by the environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5455, "margin": 0